WEBVTT

NOTE StoryCast sample captions for Threads of Dawn. Timed from synthesised narration.

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.990
<v Narrator>Before the market opens, the loom is already awake.

2
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:10.843
<v Narrator>In Iseyin, Mama Folake weaves aso oke, the heavy cloth worn at weddings and naming ceremonies.

3
00:00:11.493 --> 00:00:16.223
<v Mama Folake>My grandmother taught me to count the threads with my fingers, not my eyes.

4
00:00:16.873 --> 00:00:22.831
<v Narrator>Each strip is only as wide as a hand. Many strips are sewn together into one cloth.

5
00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:28.890
<v Mama Folake>One wedding cloth can take three weeks. People ask why I do not use a machine.

6
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.819
<v Mama Folake>A machine can make cloth. It cannot make a memory.

7
00:00:33.469 --> 00:00:38.092
<v Narrator>Now her granddaughter sits at the second loom, learning the rhythm of the shuttle.

8
00:00:38.392 --> 00:00:41.664
<v Narrator>The pattern grows, one careful row at a time.
